<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $362.9 mln June 16.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $362.9 mln June 16.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $362.9 million surplus on June 16 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank.</p>
<p>Dealers estimated that around $360 million of financial buys was due to a Eurobond issue by Sao Paulo state electrical firm Cesp.</p>
<p>The Central Bank issued the following breakdown:</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON JUNE 16</p>
<p>Exports: $249.4 million</p>
<p>Imports: $275.2 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $712.8 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $324.1 million</p>
<p>Net surplus: $362.9 million</p>
<p>JUNE DOLLAR FLOWS UP DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $2.482 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $2.879 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $4.477 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $3.798 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $282 million</p>
<p>Note: Figures rounded off.</p>
<p>((--Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroon, 55 11 2485418))</p>
</text>
